"Equip/stance menus key each armament button by entityId, but the click handler (toggledAssetIds) and every loadout config component store ASSET ids (Vec<u32>). The counted-multiset rule (countedAssets.ts) then lights the first N instances by entity id, so clicking the 2nd of two identical items turns on the 1st — the click and the highlight disagree. Same bug class as the delivered bug-duplicate-armor-instances-both-draw-equipped, resurfacing on the click path because the fix there was display-only. Real fix: config components (default_armaments, stance loadouts, relics, armor) select specific INVENTORY ENTITIES by id, not asset-id counts. Canonical EquipmentComponent can stay asset-id based (stats are fungible); reconciliation resolves chosen entity ids -> asset stat blocks. Eliminates the counted-multiset machinery entirely: highlight becomes set.has(entityId), ownership validation and config sanitation become exact by entity id. DECISION NEEDED: config-entities-only vs canonical-equipment-also-entity-id."